on.","timestamp":1785220427629063001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Continuation milestone for epic 94d9-f225-844c-43e5: story 1934 is merged and closed. next-batch reports ready leaf stories 749c-7546-6fe3-4d27 and 1fd4-cebe-87e9-4937 as SKIPPED_NEEDS_PLANNING because the scheduler intentionally batches task-level work only. Current authoring guidance explicitly defines any childless ticket, including a story, as an executable leaf; rebar-implement forbids inventing decomposition. Therefore preserve the existing planned story leaves, use ready/dependency order directly, and take numbered S2 749c next. Tests will assert observable behavior/contracts only, never source text or private structure.","timestamp":1785220567710604001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation for story 749c: first review BLOCKED on missing data flow from ticket file_impact_scope to build_manifest and an ungrounded resign claim. Revised the ticket before claim to specify sign_plan_review as the store-read/classification boundary; manifest.py remains dependency-light; build_manifest receives a backward-compatible file_scope keyword; resign_plan_review inherits behavior through its existing signer call. Also pinned none-only fingerprint encoding, legacy and rollback semantics, drift-floor ordering rationale, public helper exports, the 800-line cap, and behavior/contract-only tests. Updated file impact to include the three observable-contract test modules; removed the unsupported plan_review.__init__ change.","timestamp":1785221452867728001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD contract card for 749c (authoritative contract: signed ticket plan + epic ACs). Preconditions: story claimed; S1 exposes undeclared/paths/none state; old empty-deps records use whole-HEAD freshness. Production paths: pure build_manifest/manifest reader contract; real temporary git+ticket store+SSHSIG verification into compute_validity; public current_material_fingerprint over ticket transitions; public resign_plan_review into signature verification. Tiers: unit contract tests for pure serialization/classification; integration tests with real git/store/signature where a lower mocked tier cannot prove authenticated-manifest authority or HEAD movement. Postconditions: none stays certified across unrelated HEAD drift; unscoped/legacy/malformed stay stale-head; plaintext tamper cannot forge none; scope/reason changes stale material; recovery re-sign authenticates none. Negative controls: paths preserve legacy bytes and dependency behavior; undeclared and future tokens remain fail-closed. Collateral invariants: legacy fingerprints and manifests remain byte-identical; other validity dimensions remain active. CI gate: exact nodes under make test, plus full make test. No fault-recovery contract applies. Every assertion observes return values, signed payloads, persisted ticket state, or serialized public contracts; no source grep/private-registry assertions.","timestamp":1785222357247088001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"749c RED evidence: selected oracle run collected and executed 138 tests under the make-test pytest tier; 127 existing tests passed and 11 new tests failed for the intended missing behavior. Failures were TypeError for absent build_manifest(file_scope), AttributeError for absent public classifier/reader, none fingerprint equal to undeclared, none signed record returning stale-head after real HEAD movement, and recovered signature lacking readable none scope. Unscoped/malformed controls and existing tests stayed green. No syntax/import/fixture/setup failure. Next: remove held-out edge/integration tests from the worktree, leave only public manifest+fingerprint happy-path tests, dispatch a separate standard-tier implementer, then restore the full oracle.","timestamp":1785222550930722001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"749c held-out validation: standard-tier implementer attempt 1 passed both visible tests, 106 neighboring tests, typecheck, touched-file Ruff/format, and module-size checks (attest 799, manifest 484, pass1 568). After restoring the physically withheld oracle, all 138 selected tests passed on first run. Defect-seeded mutation restored the old whole-HEAD fallback for none: the real signed-record HEAD-drift test failed with valid=False, then passed after exact restoration. Refactoring litmus passes: tests observe public return values, authenticated signed payloads, persisted state, and stable serialization/fingerprint contracts; no assertion depends on helper call order, private registry contents, or source text.","timestamp":1785222936674901001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"749c code review: fresh-context gpt-5.6-sol reviewer APPROVED with no Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit findings. Reviewed authenticated scope parsing, fail-closed malformed/duplicate handling, legacy manifest bytes, signing classification, DEFAULT validity ordering, none-only material fingerprints, public resign behavior, and behavior/contract-focused tests. Independent verification: 138 targeted tests, module-size tests, lint/format, mypy, and diff-check passed; attest.py is 799 lines. Proceeding to exact project gates.","timestamp":1785223554823852001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"749c exact preflight gates PASS: make lint (ruff check + format-check, DCO identity, zizmor, actionlint), make typecheck (381 source files), make test (7339 passed, 29 skipped, 114 deselected, 13 warnings in 1691.76s). Full held-out oracle previously 138/138 green; defect mutation proven red and restored green. Ready to commit for Gerrit.","timestamp":1785225900105561001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"749c pushed to Gerrit change 995: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/995 . Commit a4ce23b48 carries rebar-ticket trailer, DCO sign-off, and Change-Id Ie667a3b5cd1645a5cb8855269f793b12ad2bf0dc. Awaiting mandatory LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments before submit.","timestamp":1785226041314867001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Story 1fd4 pre-claim review BLOCKED on incorrect prompt-index target and missing overlay/pass1 data-flow scope. Revised plan/file impact to remove generated reviewers/index.json, add criteria/overlay.py and pass1.py, specify structured declared_reason flow, and require behavior/contract tests with no source-grep/change-detector assertions. Re-review pending; story remains open and unclaimed.","timestamp":1785227850132708001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Story 749c change 995 earned LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and merged as 6ec1ad21. GitHub CI run 30341074857 succeeded. origin/main now contains the Gerrit trivial rebase; continuing from a fresh worktree rather than rewriting the obsolete local patch commit.","timestamp":1785228004387168001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Continuation moved to clean post-merge worktree implement-94d9-tristate-s3. Session-log helper rotated to e464-371d-cf28-43a5; that log is linked to epic 94d9-f225-844c-43e5. Story 749c is merged, completion-verified PASS, and closed.","timestamp":1785229012767867001}],"created_at":1785219484520827001,"creati